<item>
            <title>[LU-20842] LNet: Peer discovery ping/push concurrency ref leak</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20842</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;h4&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Description&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Description&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A peer with both `lp_ping_mdh` and `lp_push_mdh` outstanding gets both unlinked by `lnet_peer_cancel_discovery()` during queue cleanup 1. `LNetMDUnlink()` only delivers the unlink event inline when `md_refcount == 0`; a busy MD defers it to the LND completion path. The inline event moves the peer off `ln_dc_expired`, so cleanup 2 stops waiting and cleanup 3 dequeues it via `lnet_peer_discovery_complete(lp, -ESHUTDOWN)` &#8212; which sets `LNET_PEER_REDISCOVER`, so `lnet_peer_is_uptodate()` stays false. When the deferred event finally arrives, `lnet_peer_queue_for_discovery()` finds `lp_dc_list` empty, takes a fresh ref, and puts the peer back on `ln_dc_request`, ultimately causing a reference leak.&#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Triggerconditions%26timing&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Trigger conditions &amp;amp; timing&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;p&gt;1. A peer has both `lp_ping_mdh` and `lp_push_mdh` outstanding;&lt;br/&gt;
2. `lnet_peer_cancel_discovery()` triggers unlink of both MDs during queue cleanup 1;&lt;br/&gt;
3. The unlink includes one inline if idle and one deferred event if busy;&lt;br/&gt;
4. The inline unlink completes cleanup 2 and cleanup 3, and drains the queue;&lt;br/&gt;
5. If the deferred unlink arrives afterward, it re-inserts the peer into `ln_dc_request`, and this reference will never be released, causing a leak.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Impact%26errors&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Impact &amp;amp; errors&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;p&gt;1. May trigger `LASSERT(list_empty(&amp;amp;the_lnet.ln_dc_request))`;&lt;br/&gt;
2. May report &quot;Memory leaks detected&quot; at module unload;&lt;br/&gt;
3. May trigger `LASSERT(md-&amp;gt;md_handler != handler)` in `lnet_assert_handler_unused()`.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Once the erroneous timing window is hit, a reference leak occurs; the final error point depends on the concurrency timing of the peer re-inserting and the detection point.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
